# THE MINT GATE'S PIN (BUILD-DELTA #36; the Hypervisor Director's ruling "Batch-3 Codex r5 = FAIL" and the IOI
# Director's amendments (1) and (2); Codex batch-3 r6's MAJOR 2 and the IOI Director's 2026-10-14 amendment (2)): the
# deny list (clippy.toml) the per-dependency review (DEPENDENCY-REVIEW.md) CONFIRMED for exactly this set; the features
# of the inventoried packages (a new one fails the gate until the shipped feature set that uses it is a `config`); the
# CONFIGURATIONS the gate checks (every shipped feature set of ioi-node: the default daemon build, the CI node profile
# of .github/actions/prebuild-node-profile, the four distribution profiles; and every feature in TWO builds, since
# ioi-node's commitment features are mutually exclusive and --all-features does not build: all-hash = every feature
# whose closure does not enable commitment-kzg, all-kzg = every feature whose closure does not enable commitment-hash,
# each with every ioi-services feature); the direct normal dependencies of ioi-node and ioi-services under default
# features and under every feature; and, from cargo metadata (--offline --locked) of EVERY configuration, normalized
# and sorted: the feature FORWARDING (`forward <package> <feature> <forwarded>`) and the dependency feature SELECTIONS
# (`select <package> <dependency> <kind> <target> <optional|required> default-features=<yes|no> <features>`) of every
# workspace package the inventoried build reaches, and the RESOLVED features (`resolved <configurations|*>
# <package@version> <features>`) of every package it reaches over normal and build edges (- = none). Any change to a
# line here, or to clippy.toml, fails the gate by name until the review is re-done for the new set. Generated by
# work/s1-security/b3r/bin/gen_depspin3.py from the gate's own print.
